// JobCompletionIssue Why a COMPLETED job delivered no document.
//
// Read for what a run did; the verdict only says whether anything was lost. A run whose
// source handed back nothing finishes `processing_status: SUCCESS` with an empty
// destination, and without this there is no statement anywhere that it moved nothing
// (Pylon 2287, PLU-622). A run that discovered documents and delivered none of them
// without failing any is FAILED, and carries this for the same reason: nothing else on the
// row explains it. A run whose documents failed carries none of these; `/failed-files`
// explains it.
//
// So the verdict cannot be used to find these runs, and a caller that wants to know
// whether a job delivered anything branches on this field.
//
// Its own type on its own nullable field, deliberately NOT a `JobProcessingStatus`
// member: that enum is on the public wire and a closed generated-SDK enum breaks a
// whole `list_jobs` page on one unrecognised value (DTPL-696, `REJECTED`).
//
// Null is "no issue detected", never "checked and fine" -- a caller must not read the
// absence of a value as a guarantee, and a job FAILED for some other reason (a failed
// document, a preflight rejection) carries none of these. New members may be added; treat
// an unrecognised one as "an issue was detected, of a kind this client does not know".
type JobCompletionIssue string

